<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-6">6 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth II becomes Queen on the death of George VI</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 25-year-old princess learned of her father's death while in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kenya">Kenya</a>. She reigned for 70 years, the longest of any British monarch, until her death in 2022.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-28">28 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japan regains its sovereignty as the Allied occupation ends</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-san-francisco">Treaty of San Francisco</a> came into force, ending the Allied occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> that had begun in 1945. A US-Japan security treaty took effect the same day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-23">23 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Egypt's Free Officers overthrow King Farouk</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Army officers led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-naguib">Muhammad Naguib</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser">Gamal Abdel Nasser</a> seized power in a bloodless coup, forcing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farouk-of-egypt">King Farouk</a> to abdicate days later. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> became a republic in 1953.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bolivian-national-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolivian-national-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bolivian-national-revolution">Bolivian National Revolution</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bolivian National Revolution began in April 1952, when the Revolutionary Nationalist Movement (MNR) of Víctor Paz Estenssoro, backed by armed miners and workers, overthrew the military government.</p></div></li></ol></section>
