<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-bolivia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Bolivia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Bolivia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The National Revolution brings universal suffrage and nationalises the mines</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Guatemala.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Guatemala</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jacobo Árbenz enacts the agrarian reform of Decree 900</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-luxembourg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Grand%20Duchy%20of%20Luxembourg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Grand Duchy of Luxembourg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The High Authority of the European Coal and Steel Community settles in Luxembourg</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/lapita-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lapita%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lapita culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Edward Gifford and Richard Shutler excavate the site of Lapita in New Caledonia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/mycenaean-civilisation"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mycenaean%20civilisation.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mycenaean civilisation</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Michael Ventris deciphers Linear B, showing that it records Greek</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/anti-apartheid-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anti-apartheid%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anti-apartheid movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The ANC and the South African Indian Congress launch the Defiance Campaign against Unjust Laws</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-turkey"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Turkey.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Turkey</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After fighting with the UN forces in the Korean War, Turkey joins NATO as a bulwark against Soviet expansion into the Mediterranean.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-cuba-1902-1959"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Cuba%20(1902-1959).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Cuba (1902-1959)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Batista seizes power in a coup before the presidential election, suspends the 1940 constitution and revokes most political liberties.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/nelson-mandela"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nelson%20Mandela.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nelson Mandela</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He opens the Defiance Campaign at a Durban rally, is arrested, and is elected president of the ANC's Transvaal branch</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dead-sea-scrolls"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dead%20Sea%20Scrolls.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dead Sea Scrolls</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Cave 4, by far the most productive of the caves, was found and excavated</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/cairo"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Cairo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Cairo</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Cairo Fire destroys nearly 700 shops, cinemas, casinos and hotels in the Downtown</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/palenque"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Palenque.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Palenque</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Alberto Ruz Lhuillier opens the passage to Pakal's tomb</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/united-states-declaration-of-independence"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20States%20Declaration%20of%20Independence.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United States Declaration of Independence</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The engrossed Declaration is transferred to the National Archives, where it is on permanent display</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-mau-rebellion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20Mau%20rebellion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau Mau rebellion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Senior Chief Waruhiu is shot on 9 October and the State of Emergency is declared on 20 October</span></li></ul></section>
